# v0.4.0 placeholder. Real scripts (TWO host platforms supported):
#
#   setup-android.ps1       — Win11 host. winget install Google.PlatformTools,
#                             Python venv, asks ADB mode, registers Task Scheduler.
#   setup-android.sh        — macOS host. brew install android-platform-tools,
#                             Python venv, asks ADB mode, registers launchd.
#   _launch-android.{ps1,sh}— Per-host launcher invoked by the auto-start service.
#   diagnose-android.{ps1,sh}— Per-host diagnostic (adb devices / port-listen /
#                             scrcpy probe), mirrors windows diagnose.ps1.
#
# ADB connection mode (USB / Wireless / Hybrid) is asked at install time
# by the setup script and recorded in ~/.atb-android/config.toml. The
# MCP server itself is connection-mode agnostic: it just trusts that
# `adb devices` shows the target phone.
